WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.979
A burger covered in gold.

00:00:02.212 --> 00:00:04.061
A truffle that once sold for over

00:00:04.081 --> 00:00:05.856
three hundred thousand dollars.

00:00:06.148 --> 00:00:08.097
A dessert that comes with diamonds.

00:00:08.272 --> 00:00:09.850
And it's all one dinner.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:11.753
Welcome to Billionaire Bites.

00:00:11.773 --> 00:00:13.049
Our vision is simple:

00:00:13.341 --> 00:00:15.190
to take you inside the world's most

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:18.023
extraordinary food, where every dish is jewelry

00:00:18.043 --> 00:00:19.973
on a plate, and every price has

00:00:19.993 --> 00:00:20.979
a story.

00:00:21.509 --> 00:00:23.242
Tonight, one table in a dark dining

00:00:23.262 --> 00:00:24.887
room is set for a single guest.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.081
His order to the chef was simple:

00:00:27.372 --> 00:00:29.453
cook me the most expensive dinner on

00:00:29.473 --> 00:00:30.204
Earth.

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:31.979
The chef has one night,

00:00:31.999 --> 00:00:33.612
and a menu of five courses.

00:00:33.904 --> 00:00:35.555
Every ingredient must come from the best

00:00:35.575 --> 00:00:36.526
place in the world.

00:00:36.887 --> 00:00:38.454
So the journey begins.

00:00:38.984 --> 00:00:40.508
Course one begins in a field at

00:00:40.528 --> 00:00:41.154
dawn.

00:00:41.515 --> 00:00:43.434
One gram of saffron takes about one

00:00:43.454 --> 00:00:45.171
hundred and fifty flowers.

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:47.422
Each flower blooms for only a few

00:00:47.442 --> 00:00:49.686
days a year, and holds just three

00:00:49.706 --> 00:00:50.913
crimson threads.

00:00:51.274 --> 00:00:52.810
Every thread is picked by hand,

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:54.442
before the sun can fade it.

00:00:54.972 --> 00:00:56.980
The threads are slowly dried,

00:00:57.004 --> 00:00:59.499
until deep red turns to liquid gold.

00:00:59.953 --> 00:01:01.136
Did you already know?

00:01:01.497 --> 00:01:02.893
That is why saffron is the most

00:01:02.913 --> 00:01:04.549
expensive spice on Earth.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:05.966
Back in the kitchen,

00:01:05.986 --> 00:01:07.452
the chef soaks the threads in warm

00:01:07.472 --> 00:01:08.028
milk.

00:01:08.389 --> 00:01:10.633
Good to know: this releases the color

00:01:10.653 --> 00:01:12.537
and flavor, so a pinch can paint

00:01:12.557 --> 00:01:13.961
a whole pot of rice.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:16.149
The first plate reaches the table,

00:01:16.382 --> 00:01:17.554
golden and fragrant.

00:01:17.845 --> 00:01:18.924
One course down.

00:01:19.471 --> 00:01:21.018
Now the chef needs something from the

00:01:21.038 --> 00:01:21.931
forest.

00:01:22.461 --> 00:01:24.066
Course two begins at night,

00:01:24.086 --> 00:01:26.082
in an Italian forest near Alba.

00:01:26.443 --> 00:01:28.478
Hunters rely on trained dogs to sniff

00:01:28.498 --> 00:01:29.670
out the white truffle,

00:01:29.729 --> 00:01:31.249
hidden among tree roots.

00:01:31.779 --> 00:01:33.659
Nobody has ever farmed it reliably.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:35.660
This ugly lump of dirt can cost

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:37.471
more than gold, and its aroma fades

00:01:37.491 --> 00:01:38.616
within days.

00:01:39.147 --> 00:01:40.481
Did you already know?

00:01:40.772 --> 00:01:42.668
One giant white truffle once sold for

00:01:42.688 --> 00:01:44.638
over three hundred thousand dollars.

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:47.395
So the truffle races to the kitchen,

00:01:47.454 --> 00:01:49.176
and is shaved fresh over a warm

00:01:49.196 --> 00:01:49.798
plate.

00:01:50.252 --> 00:01:51.927
Good to know: truffles are never really

00:01:51.947 --> 00:01:52.504
cooked.

00:01:52.795 --> 00:01:54.087
The heat of the dish is enough

00:01:54.107 --> 00:01:55.673
to wake up the aroma.

00:01:56.203 --> 00:01:58.060
Course three comes from Japan.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.858
Real Kobe beef comes only from Hyogo,

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:02.534
and every cut is tracked from farm

00:02:02.554 --> 00:02:03.458
to plate.

00:02:03.989 --> 00:02:06.291
It's A5 wagyu, the highest grade of

00:02:06.311 --> 00:02:07.216
beef on Earth.

00:02:07.391 --> 00:02:09.352
Inspectors score the marbling,

00:02:09.481 --> 00:02:10.900
those white ribbons of fat,

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.220
from one to twelve.

00:02:12.749 --> 00:02:14.192
In the pan, the fat melts at

00:02:14.212 --> 00:02:16.069
a lower temperature than normal beef,

00:02:16.244 --> 00:02:17.764
so it dissolves on your tongue.

00:02:18.217 --> 00:02:20.357
Good to know: a few thin slices

00:02:20.377 --> 00:02:21.351
are enough.

00:02:21.881 --> 00:02:23.993
One steak can cost hundreds of dollars.

00:02:24.168 --> 00:02:25.762
The plate is set before the guest,

00:02:25.782 --> 00:02:27.422
but the chef is saving the boldest

00:02:27.442 --> 00:02:29.229
idea for course four.

00:02:29.759 --> 00:02:31.407
Course four is a surprise.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:33.303
The chef takes that wagyu and builds

00:02:33.323 --> 00:02:35.823
a burger, a thick patty seared until

00:02:35.843 --> 00:02:38.388
the fat glistens, on a toasted brioche

00:02:38.408 --> 00:02:39.197
bun.

00:02:39.727 --> 00:02:42.071
Next comes a spoonful of caviar,

00:02:42.246 --> 00:02:44.347
the salted eggs of the sturgeon fish.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:46.940
The rarest comes from an albino sturgeon,

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:48.647
and can cost tens of thousands of

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:49.954
dollars a kilo.

00:02:50.485 --> 00:02:52.272
The finishing touch is real,

00:02:52.447 --> 00:02:54.931
edible, twenty four karat gold leaf.

00:02:55.025 --> 00:02:56.131
Did you already know?

00:02:56.151 --> 00:02:57.129
It is so thin,

00:02:57.149 --> 00:02:58.855
it is completely edible.

00:02:59.385 --> 00:03:01.230
Good to know: gold has no taste.

00:03:01.405 --> 00:03:03.285
It simply passes through your body.

00:03:03.646 --> 00:03:05.019
You are paying for the look,

00:03:05.039 --> 00:03:06.106
and the story.

00:03:06.397 --> 00:03:07.805
Some of these burgers sell for more

00:03:07.825 --> 00:03:09.427
than a thousand dollars.

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:12.235
Before dessert, the chef serves a palate

00:03:12.255 --> 00:03:13.728
cleanser, with vanilla.

00:03:14.182 --> 00:03:16.182
Every orchid flower opens for just one

00:03:16.202 --> 00:03:18.284
day, so farmers pollinate each one by

00:03:18.304 --> 00:03:19.115
hand.

00:03:19.646 --> 00:03:21.182
And edible bird's nest,

00:03:21.202 --> 00:03:23.732
made from the dried saliva of swiftlets,

00:03:24.093 --> 00:03:27.087
prized in Chinese cooking for centuries.

00:03:27.617 --> 00:03:28.731
Notice the pattern.

00:03:29.022 --> 00:03:30.976
Hand picking, hand pollinating,

00:03:30.996 --> 00:03:32.132
hand harvesting.

00:03:32.586 --> 00:03:34.667
Luxury food is usually expensive because of

00:03:34.687 --> 00:03:37.426
human time, not just rare ingredients.

00:03:37.956 --> 00:03:39.290
Now the final course.

00:03:39.465 --> 00:03:41.496
The chef turns to the most famous

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.458
luxury dessert in the world.

00:03:43.633 --> 00:03:45.854
It was served at Serendipity 3 in

00:03:45.874 --> 00:03:48.091
New York for twenty five thousand dollars,

00:03:48.266 --> 00:03:50.227
and it set a Guinness record.

00:03:50.757 --> 00:03:53.055
The goblet is lined with edible gold,

00:03:53.079 --> 00:03:54.893
and it sits on an eighteen karat

00:03:54.913 --> 00:03:56.758
gold bracelet with diamonds.

00:03:57.289 --> 00:03:58.755
You eat it with a gold spoon

00:03:58.775 --> 00:04:00.299
set with diamonds, and you get to

00:04:00.319 --> 00:04:01.201
keep it.

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:02.971
Five courses.

00:04:03.146 --> 00:04:04.910
A spice from a flower field,

00:04:05.085 --> 00:04:06.663
a truffle from a forest,

00:04:06.954 --> 00:04:09.524
beef from Japan, a burger crowned in

00:04:09.544 --> 00:04:11.985
caviar and gold, and a dessert that

00:04:12.005 --> 00:04:13.490
doubles as jewelry.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.412
The candle burns low.

00:04:15.587 --> 00:04:16.450
The table is empty,

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:17.572
and the guest is gone.

00:04:17.933 --> 00:04:19.457
All that is left is the story

00:04:19.477 --> 00:04:21.415
of where every bite came from.

00:04:21.945 --> 00:04:23.012
Now it's your turn.

00:04:23.303 --> 00:04:24.839
If you could only pick one course

00:04:24.859 --> 00:04:27.517
from tonight's menu, which would it be?

00:04:27.692 --> 00:04:29.200
Tell us in the comments.

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:31.660
Follow Billionaire Bites for more jewelry on

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:32.272
a plate.

00:04:32.632 --> 00:04:34.075
Next time, we'll find an even more

00:04:34.095 --> 00:04:35.360
expensive menu.
